package server

const mcpSimulationPolicy = "Process Simulator is a first-class diagram type process-simulator with a separate simulation payload type:process-simulator,schemaVersion:1. GET /simulation/capabilities discovers units, limits and supported operations. GET /templates discovers browser-local template IDs: process-simulator-blank is guided empty setup, while process-simulator is the Kiosk + package pickup example. Create through POST /diagrams with {name,type:process-simulator}; this preserves the kiosk default. Build your own process by versioned PUT of an empty or complete semantic model, using the discovered template's graph.simulation or the documented schema. GET/PUT /diagrams/{diagramId}/simulation reads/replaces the complete semantic model at baseVersion; nodes, edges, particle-types, resources and scenarios have semantic CRUD under that same route. UI guided setup and connected-node additions write this same model. Shared resources, queues, complexity, routing, schedules, scaling, improvements and economic settings are explicit model fields, never inferred from canvas positions. POST /diagrams/{diagramId}/simulation/runs starts the same deterministic worker engine used by the UI with seed,durationSeconds,scenarioId,demandMultiplier,speed and animated options; it immediately returns a separately identifiable run. Poll GET .../runs/{runId}/state or /result. GET metrics, nodes/{nodeId}, resources/{resourceId}, bottlenecks and paged events inspect actual semantic state. Live green/yellow/red traffic indicators derive from current queues, currentUtilization and resource waitingNodeIds; inspect these semantic values rather than guessing from colors. travelSeconds is actual simulated transfer time; zero means instant transfer, and resource-allocation connectors never transport particles. POST pause,resume,stop,reset and seek control that run; exact POST simulation/compare compares runIds without mutating the models. Read only permits inspection and exact comparison; starting or controlling runs and model changes require Read + write. Headless/MAX execution needs no active canvas or animation loop, but the browser must remain connected for IndexedDB and local worker execution. Go and MCP have no separate simulation engine or shadow configuration. Live 2D scaling uses separate full native cards such as Counter 1/2/3: anonymous capacity units with one shared logical model, actual aggregate occupancy and a shared queue. In the full flow the original primary card edits the saved logical object; additional capacity cards and compact hierarchy placements are read-only projections. visualCapacity discovery exposes eight cards per bank and 256 additional cards globally, with explicitly labelled aggregate overflow. These cards are not separate persistent process nodes or named-worker business identities; 3D retains the logical model. Models, scenarios and bounded results remain browser-local; seeds and immutable input snapshots support deterministic replay and repeated demand stress tests." + " Run summaries expose scenarioName and currency captured by each run, independent of later document edits. Comparisons return the common captured currency; mixed currencies return structured 422 SIMULATION_CURRENCY_MISMATCH without exchange-rate conversion." + " visualCapacity exposes primaryEditable:true, additionalCardsReadOnly:true and compactHierarchyReadOnly:true. Deprecated readOnly:true applies only to additional/compact projections, not the editable original primary card." + mcpProcessHierarchyPolicy
